<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm4b-jiuquan ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 4B / Yaogan 53-07..09 + 56-19..21 (Jiuquan) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 20.00 s, kick 3.395 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.667, payload 1571 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.8346-0.002481*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: Long March 4B (sim/vehicles/lm4b.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-4B TIMELINE mode: stage data + Y51/LEO flight sequence from huijiwiki (sources: World Launch Vehicles 2nd ed. 2007, SAST); all event times hard constraints.
Terminal-velocity-trim burn (S3 &#x27;final velocity correction&#x27; to 662.684 s) not modelled: its thrust is unpublished. Insertion reported at S3 shutdown 648.684 s.
Flown: LL2 Success 19:25Z (Y81). Az 109 from ZJ385/26 + NOTAMs. Event times = published Y51/LEO Jiuquan sequence (huijiwiki), the closest published LM-4B LEO-from-Jiuquan flight; Y81&#x27;s own sequence unpublished.
Target (see launch config): insertion 500 km, apoapsis 500 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 109.00 deg; payload 1571 kg.
Pad: 40.960482N 100.298059E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-23T19:25:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (CASC/SAST did not publish Y81&#x27;s separation time; the Y51 sequence&#x27;s 14 s velocity-trim burn to T+662.7 s is also not modelled (thrust unpublished)). From insertion T+648.7 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 94.62 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast.
POST-CUTOFF end T+12003 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 499.83 km, osculating 494.9 x 505.4 km, i 45.031 deg.</description>
